  "decision": "No concrete supported correction selected; retain application and charts source",
  "observations": [
    {
      "topic": "Routes and body authorization",
      "result": "Human wrapper resolves authenticated actor and current account. Policy POST/PATCH/DELETE use fresh human engine-administrator check before their 3 MiB metadata body; preview retains generic 512 KiB. Strict full replacement policy schemas reject extra/value fields. Body deadline20s,4096chunks,10000aliases of max253 characters remain.",
      "source": "policy routes;kv-http.ts:22-68;kv-schemas.ts:3-17;kv-contract.ts:12-15"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Policy validation and metadata CAS",
      "result": "validPolicy validates normalized segment prefix, unique supported actions/effect, existing mount and principal, legacy list/read audience and 256-rule cap. Serialized accountLock transaction rechecks fresh administration. Existing policy preview/update/delete requires positive safe expected revision; missing428, invalid400, stale409 after existing-record/validation ordering. Update increments revision. Human-only create needs no legacy preview. Policy schema revision is optional to preserve deliberate registry428 enforcement, not an authorization bypass.",
      "source": "kv-registry.ts:18-73,227-285;kv-contract.ts:79-82;schema.prisma:95-105"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Legacy transitions",
      "result": "Either new or previous principal legacy-lookup triggers recomputed impact, including moving away, and delete uses prior rule. Affected set unions old/new read scopes with complete-segment prefix matching. Same effective before/after result still belongs to affected scope; list-only rules can require a valid fingerprint and empty exact set. Legacy principal revision and metadata audit are written inside the same transaction as policy mutation.",
      "source": "kv-registry.ts:243-285;kv-legacy-access.ts:38-40,86-119"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Fingerprint and pages",
      "result": "Fresh bounded alias file plus exact metadata references are validated and sorted. Snapshot includes normalized intended fields/action order, prior policy metadata, current principal/legacy rules, exact alias target rows, bindings/path and mount revisions/normalized scopes, grants and before/after authorization. Preview returns max100 rows/cursor; all pages repeat the same fingerprint only while metadata remains unchanged. No native value/digest/head request in this impact helper.",
      "source": "kv-legacy-access.ts:19-139;secret-aliases.ts;alias-catalog.ts:7-27"
    },
    {
